{
  "title": "Neuropathic (Charcot) Joint of the Elbow",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/422873/neuropathic-charcot-joint-of-the-elbow",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 6 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Neuropathic Charcot Joint of the Elbow is a chronic and progressive joint disease most commonly caused by syringomyelia leading to the destruction of the elbow joint and surrounding bony structures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with radiographs of the elbow and supplemented with cervical spine MRI to assess for a syrinx.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment should be individualized based on degree of functional limitation and underlying neurological condition. Neurosurgical decompression is indicated in the presence of a syrinx.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rare condition in the upper extremity (~ 40 cases reported in literature)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "elbow (this topic)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "shoulder",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "foot & ankle (see diabetic Charcot foot)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**syrinx formation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "syrinx formation (fluid-filled cavity) in spinal cord causes damage to the decussating fibers of the lateral spinothalamic tract leading to **loss of pain and temperature sensation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "loss of pain/temperature leads to dissociative anesthesia in which proprioception and motor function are preserved but pain and temperature are not",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "as syrinx enlarges, damage to dorsal column and anterior horn of spinal cord lead to areflexia, loss of motor strength and muscle atrophy.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**joint destruction**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422873/images/3843059e-ced8-4573-98d1-3d7f9fe47aa9_neuropathic_elbow_2..jpg",
                  "caption": "Charcot elbow with complete destruction and dislocation of elbow"
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422873/images/27d38524-10ac-4ed4-93e9-77f394df9c3c_charcot_1..jpg",
                  "caption": "Charcot elbow with complete destruction of the elbow joint"
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422873/images/bc0d6fb4-0c79-4486-821b-db09e915488c_neuropathic_elbow_3..jpg",
                  "caption": "Charcot elbow"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**neurotrauma**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "loss of peripheral sensation and proprioception leads to **repetitive microtrauma** to the joint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "poor fine motor control generates unnatural pressure on certain joints leading to additional microtrauma",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**neurovascular**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "neuropathic patients have dysregulated reflexes and desensitized joints that receive significantly **greater blood flow**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "the resulting hyperemia leads to increased **osteoclastic resorption** of bone",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "molecular biology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "RANK/RANKL/OPG triad pathway is thought to be involved",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "orthopedic conditions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**ulnar neuropathy**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "medical conditions & comorbidities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**syringomyelia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most common etiology of neuropathic arthropathy of the upper extremity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "25% of Charcot joints are a result of syringomyelia",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "monoarticular (shoulder > elbow)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**Arnold-Chiari malformation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most common cause of syringomyelia",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**Hansen's disease** (leprosy)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "second most common cause of upper extremity neuropathic arthropathy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**neurosyphilis (tabes dorsalis)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "usually affects the knee",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "can be **polyarticular**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**diabetes**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most common cause of foot and ankle neuropathic joints",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "swollen elbow",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**50% have pain, 50% are painless**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "loss of function",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "swollen, warm, erythematous joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "mimics infection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "atrophy due to ulnar nerve entrapment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "interosseous atrophy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "hypothenar atrophy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "clawing",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**loss of active motion is most common finding**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "elbow flexion, extension, pronation and supination all affected",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "elbow joint may be mechanically unstable",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "loss of passive motion indicates mechanical block",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurovascular",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "a neurologic evaluation is essential",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**ulnar nerve entrapment at the elbow very common**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "paresthesias in ulnar nerve distribution",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "interosseous weakness",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "standard views of affected joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "AP and lateral of the elbow",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "early changes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "degenerative changes may mimic osteoarthritis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "late changes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422873/images/charcot_elbow..jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422873/images/elbow_charcot..jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "obliteration of joint space",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "fragmentation of both articular surfaces of a joint leading to subluxation or dislocation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "scattered \"chunks\" of bone in fibrous tissue",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "joint distention by fluid",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "surrounding soft tissue edema",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "heterotopic ossification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "MRI of cervical spine to rule out syrinx when neuropathic elbow arthropathy is present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422873/images/syrinx..jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bone scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technetium bone scan",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "findings",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may be positive (hot) for neuropathic joints and osteomyelitis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**indium WBC scan**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "findings",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "will be negative (cold) for neuropathic joints and positive (hot) for osteomyelitis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "useful to **differentiate from osteomyelitis**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Labs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ESR and WBC can be elevated making it difficult to differentiate from osteomyelitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "EMG/NCS",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "helpful for confirming ulnar neuropathy associated with diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Histology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "synovial hypertrophy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**detritic synovitis** (cartilage and bone distributed in synovium)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteomyelitis/septic joint",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "difficult to distinguish from osteomyelitis based on radiographs and physical exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "common findings in both conditions",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "swelling, warmth",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "elevated WBC and ESR",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "technetium bone scan is \"hot\"",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "unique to Charcot joint disease",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**indium leukocyte scan will be \"cold\" (negative)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "will be \"hot\" (positive) for osteomyelitis",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rest, NSAIDs, functional bracing, restriction of activity and treatment of underlying disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line treatment for neuropathic elbow joint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "50% of patients reported improvement after non-operative management",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "intra-articular corticosteroid injection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "severe elbow pain",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "neurosurgical decompression",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "presence of cervical syrinx",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "decompression of syrinx has shown to slow disease progression, maximize joint function and improve bone quality",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "studies have shown some elbow joint space restoration following syrinx decompression",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "peripheral nerve neurolysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ulnar nerve palsies",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "PIN palsies",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "limited cases series have shown good recovery of nerve function but high recurrent rates",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "elbow arthrodesis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422873/images/elbow_arthrodesis..jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "elbow pain and instability having failed conservative management",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "limited case series have shown improvement of pain but with functional limitations",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "total joint replacement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Charcot joint is considered a contraindication to elbow total joint replacement**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "due to poor bone stock, prosthetic loosening, instability, and soft-tissue compromise",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "limited case reports exist on elbow arthroplasties for charcot elbow with mixed results",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Rest, NSAIDs, functional bracing, restriction of activity and treatment of underlying disease**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "functional bracing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "allows flexion-extension, but neutralizes varus-valgus stresses",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Intra-articular corticosteroid injection",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ulnohumeral joint injection is considered most effective",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Neurosurgical decompression",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "neurosurgical management has been reported to consist of 1 or more of the following",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "posterior fossa decompression",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "craniotomy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "syringoperitoneal shunt",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "laminectomy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Peripheral nerve neurolysis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cubital tunnel release must be performed with careful soft tissue dissection due to severely altered anatomy noted in patients with charcot elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Elbow arthrodesis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "optimal position",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "optimal position for most activities is**110 degrees flexion** whereas 45-60 degrees flexion is optimal for work-related activities.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "contoured plate fixation most commonly used to achieve arthrodesis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
